  "body": "`list_features` (`crates/app/src/mcp/features.rs`, `faces_view`) prints a planar face's `normal` and `facing` from the feature's canonical plane normal (`feature::Face.normal`), not from the face's outward side. On a plain 40 x 40 x 15 box the bottom face reads `\"normal\": [0, 0, 1], \"facing\": \"up\"` - the same as the top. Side faces pair up the same way (both Y sides read `[0, 1, 0]`).\n\nWhy it matters: an agent choosing a face for `set_wcs_from_features` (#937), `locate_part` or an operation by its `normal` / `facing` picks the wrong face half the time. For a WCS pick that is a frame turned upside down - the tools themselves read the outward normal correctly (`pick::align::outward_normal`), but the agent was steered to the wrong face. Found while writing the #937 pin, which now tells faces apart by `bounds`.\n\nDone means: a face row's `normal` (and `facing`) is the outward normal - the one `outward_normal` reads, placed where the part sits - or a refusal-shaped field when the winding is not decidable; a test pins top vs bottom and both sides of a box; the camcraft-mcp skill note about this caveat (added by #937) is removed.\n",
